    "body": "A retained city could lose its owner when the shared sixteen-word window advanced: changing the evicted owner left all parent source-candidate features identical. Each word now retains four exact predecessor identities, which the artifact-bound source selector uses outside that window. The existing learned H4 owner code becomes reachable; an outer witness reconstructs the complete e1ef0a5d parent. Numeric, admission, relation, dependent-read and emission parameters stay fixed.\n\nComplete construction improves 654/663 to 663/663 with no lost correct answer; open 12/16 to 16/16; fresh owner/query/order answers 24/32 to 32/32, while the fitted-router/window-only control remains 24/32. Exact-parent control reproduces all 663 parent outputs/stops. Initial retained-context selection already reaches 428/428 before one learned margin update. All prior preservation passes, including the earlier admission set's remaining location errors (now 12/12). These are bounded familiar-question-family results, not general language or a new angular-versus-equality claim.\n\nLocal validation: final release/offline example and focused binaries compile; seven distinct lexeme/snapshot tests, integer-kernel guard, architecture policy, actual-artifact parent/mutation/checkpoint/zero-allocation checks, formatting and claim-wording checks pass. Mismatched observation produces no derived write. Seventeen warm prediction/observation samples measure median 0.136 ms/max 0.184 ms, excluding load/encoding/ingestion/checkpoints. PR/queue statuses acknowledge compatibility only; no full-suite, public CLI rebuild, WASM, energy or frontier result is claimed.\n\nModel work 60.834 seconds; cumulative 4072.769/4170 seconds leaves 97.231 seconds. Artifact c6a98c04 is 11,626,472 bytes. Storage remains inside the predeclared 256 MiB cap; all earlier material is preserved. Snapshot validation cross-checks available overlap/token evidence while preserving legacy missing fields and unauthenticated evicted-history semantics. README, roadmap, lifecycle, research and current-state pointers now direct the next step toward reusable contextual transitions/emission conditioned on exact selected values/results.\n\nRefs #1139, #1140, #973. Full evidence: docs/native_geometric_source_context_1139.md and docs/evidence/native_geometric_source_context_1139.json.\n",
